condition_name: Liver Cirrhosis
condition_slug: liver-cirrhosis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "An advanced stage of chronic liver disease associated with histological evidence of hepatocyte degeneration, nodularity and fibrosis."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[3]: Fatigue,"Fluid retention e.g., Ascites and peripheral oedema",Peripheral stigmata of chronic liver disease.
investigations[6]: LFTs,"PT, PTTK",Liver biopsy,Ultrasound examination of the liver,Hepatitis B & C,Upper GI endoscopy.
treatment:
  goals[3]: Prevent further liver damage,Prevent deterioration of liver function,"Symptomatic relief from anaemia, fatigue and oedema"
  non_drug[3]: Encourage high fibre and low salt diet,Correction of anaemia,Reduce oedema and ascites
  drug[5]: "Diuretics: Spironolactone tablets 25 - 100 mg orally 12 hourly",Furosemide 20 - 80 mg orally 12 hourly,Salt-poor albumin for intractable ascites,"Prevention of variceal bleeding: Propranolol 40 - 80 mg orally daily",Isosorbide mononitrate 10 mg orally thrice daily
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[2]: Immunization against hepatitis A and B,Abstinence from alcohol.
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null